FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] src/parser.rs:2498 — `interpolated_parts` falls back to `literal.push('{'); index += 1` after a forward depth-count scan, so a matched-but-not-expression open rescans its whole span — nested failing braces like `"{{{x y}}}"` cost O(n) per open, O(n²) total — the doc at `src/parser.rs:2457` claims the walk is linear with disjoint scans, which is false on this shape; neither `edge_a_very_long_literal_of_braces_is_text_and_is_scanned_once` (`"{}"` pairs) nor the unmatched-opens test reaches it — time parsing a failing-nested literal of a few ten thousand opens to settle it — skip to `scan` on failure or record the failed span as consumed text.
2. [MAJOR] src/formatter.rs:759 — `InterpolatedText` writes nested expressions with raw `"` delimiters (`"{" + format_expression(part) + "}"`), and `escape_text` at `src/formatter.rs:979` only escapes direct `Text` parts — a substitution holding a string (e.g. `say "{uppercase("{x}")}"`, the nesting this phase enables) formats to outer quotes terminated early by inner quotes, which does not re-parse — run `format` on a nested-substitution program then re-`parse` it to settle it — escape inner string delimiters or refuse to format nested interpolation losslessly.
3. [MAJOR] src/lexer.rs:296 — `read_text` catch-all `Some(c) => text.push(c)` turns `\{` into `{` with no escape, so after this phase `"\{x\}"` with `x` bound substitutes (or AnalyzerErrors when unbound) where it previously printed literally as `{x}` — there is now no spelling for a literal brace pair that reads as an expression, admitted in `phases/phase-047/FINDINGS.md` §3 but untested and a silent behavior change for programs that ran yesterday — decide `\{` escapes a brace (lexer case + `escape_text` round-trip) or pin the new meaning with a test on both engines.
4. [MAJOR] bootstrap/compiler.rb:2070 — `interp_close` walks forward counting depth from every `{`, called per open at `bootstrap/compiler.rb:2128`, with no port of `unmatched_opens` — a literal of all opens costs the rest of the literal per open (quadratic), executed under the tree-walking interpreter via `rb run bootstrap/compiler.rb` — admitted in `phases/phase-047/FINDINGS.md` §6 but still ships stage-2 quadratic while stage 1 claims linear — port the backward `unmatched` pass as `interp_unmatched(b)` and consult it before `interp_close`.
REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 4
